  "texts": [
    "Sliding Window with Amortized Analysis\nFamilies: amortized_analysis\nMechanisms: two_pointers hash_lookup sliding_window monotonic_stack monotonic_queue\nSignals: subarray substring string_input minimize maximize\nOperations: subarray substring\nShapes: string_input\nGoals: minimize maximize\nComplexity: o_n o_n_squared\nFind smallest/largest window/subarray with specific properties String/array contains duplicate elements Need to track character/element frequencies Constraints mention linear time complexity Problem involves 'all unique characters' or 'contains all characters' Window needs to expand/contract based on certain conditions",
    "Level-wise Sorting in Complete Binary Trees\nFamilies: sorting\nMechanisms: sort_then_greedy comparator_sort coordinate_compression counting_sort\nSignals: subarray sort_action\nOperations: subarray sort_action\nComplexity: o_nlogn\nMention of complete binary tree in problem statement Level-order traversal mentioned or implied Requirement to process nodes level by level Need to sort elements within each level Array input representing tree nodes",
    "Greedy Problem Solving\nFamilies: greedy_algorithms\nMechanisms: two_pointers backtracking sort_then_greedy exchange_argument priority_greedy scanning_greedy\nSignals: minimize maximize dp_keyword greedy_keyword\nGoals: minimize maximize\nComplexity: o_n o_nlogn\nKeywords like 'minimum/maximum number of operations' Presence of sorted or sortable elements Matching or pairing requirements (like parentheses) Decomposition into powers or multiples Two-pointer compatible structure Unidirectional processing (left-to-right or right-to-left)",
    "XOR-based array transformation and validation\nFamilies: bit_manipulation\nMechanisms: bitmask_enumeration xor_tricks bitmask_dp shift_ops dp_on_subsets\nSignals: sort_action enumerate_permutations xor_keyword bitmask_keyword\nOperations: sort_action enumerate_permutations\nComplexity: o_n o_nlogn\nMention of bitwise XOR (⊕) in problem statement Odd integer N given as array length Requirement to reorder one array to match another's XOR properties Comparison of sorted arrays after bit manipulation Presence of binary strings and modulus operations Need to compute bitmask from array elements",
    "Binary Search on Answer with Greedy Validation\nFamilies: complete_search\nMechanisms: bitmask_enumeration backtracking dfs_enumeration bfs_enumeration branch_and_bound\nSignals: minimize maximize greedy_keyword\nGoals: minimize maximize\nComplexity: o_n o_n_squared\nKeywords like 'minimum possible maximum' or 'maximize the minimum' Constraints that can be checked with a linear scan Upper/lower bounds mentioned in problem (e.g., sum of array, max element) Partitioning continuous segments with constraints Time/space constraints that rule out brute force",
    "Linked List Traversal and String Conversion\nFamilies: data_structures\nMechanisms: monotonic_stack monotonic_queue heap_maintenance union_find hash_lookup stack_simulation queue_simulation balanced_bst priority_greedy fenwick_tree segment_tree\nSignals: construct\nGoals: construct\nComplexity: o_n\nLinked list structure provided in problem statement Requirement to output node values in order Mention of string concatenation with separators Termination condition involving null/None pointer",
    "Greedy Interval Scheduling with Sorting\nFamilies: greedy_algorithms sorting\nMechanisms: sort_then_greedy exchange_argument priority_greedy scanning_greedy comparator_sort coordinate_compression counting_sort\nSignals: enumerate_permutations interval_list_input minimize maximize greedy_keyword\nOperations: enumerate_permutations\nShapes: interval_list_input\nGoals: minimize maximize\nComplexity: o_1 o_nlogn\nPresence of intervals/ranges with start and end points Requirement to select one value per interval without collisions Guarantee that a valid solution exists within constraints Output can be any valid permutation of assignments Constraints mention 'at most one event per day' or similar uniqueness requirement",
    "State Transition DP with Constraints\nFamilies: dynamic_programming\nMechanisms: bitmask_dp state_transition_dp dp_on_indices dp_on_subsets dp_on_tree knapsack digit_dp interval_dp\nSignals: dp_keyword\nProblem involves moving between states with transition costs Constraints on valid transitions (e.g., color changes, increasing values) Need to track accumulated quantity (e.g., candies collected) Optimal substructure property present Overlapping subproblems identified",
    "Prefix Sum and Difference Array Techniques\nFamilies: range_queries\nMechanisms: prefix_sum difference_array fenwick_tree segment_tree sparse_table offline_queries mo_algorithm coordinate_compression\nSignals: range_update prefix_keyword\nOperations: range_update\nComplexity: o_1 o_n o_n_squared\nMentions of 'sum of elements between indices' Requests to find pivot/balance points in arrays Operations involve adding/subtracting values over ranges Need to track cumulative effects of multiple range operations Problem constraints prohibit naive O(n^2) solutions",
    "Two-pointer greedy pairing with amortized analysis\nFamilies: amortized_analysis greedy_algorithms\nMechanisms: two_pointers sliding_window monotonic_stack monotonic_queue sort_then_greedy exchange_argument priority_greedy scanning_greedy\nSignals: sort_action minimize maximize greedy_keyword\nOperations: sort_action\nGoals: minimize maximize\nComplexity: o_1 o_n o_nlogn\nExplicit capacity limit for groups/pairs Each group can contain at most 2 elements Weight/size constraints on combinations Minimization of total groups/pairs objective Input elements have comparable attributes (weights, sizes, etc.) Problem allows or requires sorting of input"
